  "notes": "GAAP (modified accrual) per the combined Statement of Governmental Fund Revenues, Expenditures and Changes in Fund Balances and Statement of Activities (p2, original report p7, gained in the v7 re-trim). Receipts/disbursements and fund balances (5,678,646 / 4,178,612) from its Total governmental funds column (General + Construction); the reconciling-items and Statement of Activities columns are not used (net position 6,693,263 beginning / 3,951,845 ending; depreciation 2,216,224 appears only there). Warrants issued 3,594,968 as debt_proceeds. Roll-forward: 5,678,646+11,299,819-16,394,821+3,594,968=4,178,612. Collection fees are printed as a negative revenue line and kept so (property tax, review). Previously (old trim had only Schedule 1) receipts/disbursements came from Schedule 1 and its budgetary fund balances 5,220,465 / 4,604,269 were used as beginning/ending cash; those Schedule 1 lines now sit in detail (budgetary basis, Actual and budget columns, p3; differs from the GAAP statement), and beginning cash is null (no prior-year balance sheet). Read pages 1-3 of 3. Balance sheet from the combined Balance Sheet - Governmental Funds and Statement of Net Position (p1, original report p6, gained in the v8 re-trim), Statement of Net Position column (warrants and bonds split by the printed due dates; accrued interest as accrued liabilities; fund-column deferred revenue and fund balances reconcile to '---' there). ending_cash = Cash on deposit with County Treasurer 534,290 and ending_investments = Investments 4,104,162 (Total governmental funds column, same as the Statement of Net Position column)."
